## A. Universal Command Center

[A Smart Search Command Bar UI Design by Lakshay Nagpal on Dribbble](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/maSNpgIEvA0VIfquUGx7GXsGcmWuN1IlRprtWP3_KzcTKp4VOr-0H0EnwCxDkSduEJspv8dSyzEvKqEjRFHgOeq_RTO1pub_xn3vviadvPojGM4olKF5u0r55kTj8K_refr9aqXsRVVFGQO4sBH56JuyaOEqoYbI_deQ0b3sFac?purpose=inline)

Purpose: One entry point for the entire platform.

Instead of opening Student Hub, then searching for a quiz generator, the user could type:

"Create a 20-question quiz from my saved biology notes and schedule a revision session."

It should:

- Understand natural-language requests.
- Identify the intended module and task.
- Ask follow-up questions only when necessary.
- Choose the appropriate model, data source and tools.
- Show a preview of actions that change data or affect external services.
- Execute approved actions and report results.
- Provide links to the artifacts it creates.

Why it matters: It turns the many modules into one coherent experience.

## B. Memory & Knowledge Center

This is different from ordinary chat history.

| Component            | What it does                                                     |
| -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Conversation history | Saves and retrieves previous chats                               |
| User memory          | Stores approved preferences and useful recurring context         |
| Project memory       | Tracks decisions, files and progress for individual projects     |
| Knowledge base       | Indexes documents and reference material                         |
| Knowledge graph      | Connects related concepts, projects and sources                  |
| Memory controls      | Lets users inspect, correct, export and delete saved information |

Example: if a user works on a coding project over several weeks, SARVAGYA should be able to retrieve the project's architecture, known errors and previous decisions without requiring the user to explain everything again.

Memory should be permission-based, searchable and editable. It must not silently turn every conversation into permanent memory.

## C. AI Agents & Automation Center

A chatbot answers questions. An agent can work through a sequence of steps toward a goal.

### Example: Automated study workflow

1\. Gather

Find the selected notes and relevant source material.

2\. Understand

Summarize the chapter and identify important concepts.

3\. Create

Generate flashcards and a practice test.

4\. Organize

Save the material and propose a revision schedule.

The automation engine should support:

- Multi-step tasks.
- Scheduled runs.
- Task queues and progress tracking.
- Retry and recovery after errors.
- Cancellation and pause controls.
- Logs of actions and results.
- Permission checks before consequential actions.
- Human approval for sending messages, publishing, purchases or other sensitive operations.

This is one of the most important additions because it lets SARVAGYA use its other capabilities rather than merely describe them.

## D. AI Workspace

A shared working environment for all created material.

Include:

- Notes and documents.
- Tasks and projects.
- Calendar and reminders.
- File management.
- Saved AI responses.
- Tables and spreadsheets.
- Presentations.
- Whiteboards and diagrams.
- Version history.
- Project-specific AI context.

For example, the output of Web Navigator could be turned into a research document, which could then become a presentation in Creator Studio.

## E. Developer Hub

Your platform needs a dedicated environment for software development, especially because SARVAGYA itself is a software project.

Include:

- AI coding assistant.
- Code editor with syntax highlighting.
- Code explanation and debugging.
- Repository and Git integration.
- Test generation and execution.
- API testing.
- Database inspection.
- Logs and error tracing.
- Sandboxed code execution.
- Deployment integrations.

Code execution must be isolated and resource-limited. The AI should not automatically receive unrestricted access to the host operating system or secrets.

## F. Trust & Security Center

Security should be a platform-wide system, not just a settings page.

Include:

- Account and session controls.
- Role-based permissions.
- Data export and deletion.
- Connected-service permissions.
- Audit logs.
- Rate limiting and abuse protection.
- Secret and API-key management.
- Prompt-injection defenses for retrieved web content.
- User-visible AI citations and uncertainty.
- Backups and recovery.

This becomes especially important once agents, plugins, files and external APIs can interact.

