### Four kinds of improvement

Knowledge improvement: add new, properly sourced information to the retrieval index.

Workflow improvement: improve task planning, routing, caching and retries based on measured results.

Model improvement: evaluate model configurations, prompts and supported fine-tuning processes against fixed benchmarks.

Software improvement: create code changes, test them in a controlled environment, review them, deploy them in stages and retain rollback capability.

A successful system does not need to change its code every second. It needs to identify useful improvements, validate them and avoid regressions.

