## The five non-negotiable principles

1. One shared intelligence layer: every module should use common services instead of building its own disconnected AI.
2. Real information: live data must come from real, authorized sources with clear timestamps and appropriate citations.
3. Persistent operation: important background jobs and project state must survive page refreshes, connection loss and server restarts.
4. Controlled evolution: memory and knowledge can update continuously; changes to models, prompts and software must be evaluated and appropriately approved.
5. Trustworthy behavior: SARVAGYA must distinguish real results from simulations, disclose uncertainty, protect user data and report failures honestly.

